      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(google): add typed Gemini CLI auth boundary",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe bundled Google plugin has two separate auth/runtime surfaces that need a hard boundary:\n\n- `google` is the API-backed Google provider and uses API-key credentials.\n- `google-gemini-cli` is the direct Gemini CLI runtime/provider and uses OAuth credentials staged into the Gemini CLI auth home.\n\nBefore this patch, the Gemini CLI prepare path depended on a private raw auth-profile object side channel, and the bridge accepted credential shapes that could blur the boundary between Google API-key usage and Gemini CLI OAuth usage.\n\nThis PR adds a typed Google credential resolver and an explicit CLI backend auth-forwarding capability so these credential kinds cannot cross that boundary by accident.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Adds typed Google credential resolution in `src/agents/auth-profiles/google.ts`.\n- Resolves `google` only as API-key credentials.\n- Resolves `google-gemini-cli` only as OAuth credentials.\n- Adds explicit CLI backend auth-forwarding metadata for the Gemini CLI backend.\n- Changes CLI run preparation to forward credentials only when the backend capability accepts the selected provider and credential kind.\n- Fails closed when a selected profile cannot be resolved into a typed credential before crossing the CLI backend plugin boundary.\n- Removes API-key staging from the Gemini CLI OAuth bridge.\n- Preserves current-main queued/atomic Gemini staging by keeping profile-home/settings/OAuth file writes inside `beforeExecution` and writing JSON through same-directory temp-file rename.\n- Keeps Gemini CLI auth material in an isolated auth home and clears inherited Google/Gemini auth environment variables.\n- Preserves default bundled `google-gemini-cli` provider/backend registration.\n- Removes stale `OPENCLAW_ENABLE_GOOGLE_GEMINI_CLI_HARNESS` metadata/hints and deletes the unused harness opt-in helper/test.\n- Updates the Google onboarding hint so it covers both Gemini API key and Gemini CLI OAuth choices.\n- Documents CLI auth-profile forwarding in `docs/plugins/cli-backend-plugins.md` and validates the Plugin SDK API baseline.\n- Adds `scripts/proof-google-auth-replacement.ts` as a deterministic real behavior proof.\n\n## Evidence\n\nReal environment: local OpenClaw checkout at PR head `9ccfc51c30cb20cbd6f864b015f7571f73b59dfd` using production resolver, CLI prepare, Gemini CLI auth-home staging code, bundled Google plugin registration code, Plugin SDK API baseline check, stale-policy grep check, focused Vitest suites, and the permanent real behavior proof script.\n\nCommands run after the final queued-staging repair:\n\n`git diff --check`\n\n`grep -RIn -- 'OPENCLAW_ENABLE_GOOGLE_GEMINI_CLI_HARNESS\\|shouldEnableGoogleGeminiCliHarness' extensions docs src scripts package.json 2>/dev/null`\n\n`pnpm plugin-sdk:api:check`\n\n`pnpm vitest run src/agents/auth-profiles/google.test.ts src/agents/cli-runner/prepare.test.ts extensions/google/index-harness-registration.test.ts extensions/google/setup-api.test.ts src/plugin-sdk/provider-catalog-shared.test.ts`\n\n`pnpm tsx scripts/proof-google-auth-replacement.ts`\n\nObserved result:\n\n```text\nplugin-sdk:api:check OK\n7 test files passed\n155 tests passed\nreal behavior proof passed\nstale opt-in grep produced no output\ngit diff --check produced no output\n```\n\nFinal repair commit:\n\n```text\n9ccfc51c30 fix(google): preserve queued OAuth-only staging boundary\n5 files changed, 66 insertions(+), 97 deletions(-)\n```\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\nThe permanent proof script exercises the production Google credential resolver and Gemini CLI auth-home staging boundary and verifies:\n\n- `google` selects an API-key credential.\n- `google-gemini-cli` selects an OAuth credential.\n- Gemini CLI uses an isolated auth home.\n- Inherited Google auth environment variables are cleared.\n- Google API-key material is not written into Gemini CLI OAuth files.\n- Proof output redacts token values.\n- The Gemini CLI auth-home path uses a hashed profile ID.\n- The raw profile ID is absent from the auth-home path.\n- The selected credential kinds are exactly `google=api_key` and `google-gemini-cli=oauth`.\n- The proof calls queued `beforeExecution` staging before reading staged OAuth files.\n\nThe focused Vitest suite covers:\n\n- default bundled Gemini CLI provider/backend registration is preserved.\n- resolver provider/kind separation.\n- CLI prepare capability-gated credential forwarding.\n- API-key rejection by the Gemini CLI OAuth bridge.\n- non-Gemini backend unresolved/raw credential blocking.\n- no forwarding for backends without `authProfileForwarding`.\n- provider catalog/runtime contract behavior after removing stale opt-in policy references.\n- selected Gemini CLI OAuth fallback behavior after the upstream merge.\n- same-directory atomic Gemini JSON staging through temp-file rename.\n- OAuth-only staging behavior after dropping Gemini CLI API-key staging.\n\n## Final Branch State\n\nFinal pushed commit: `9ccfc51c30cb20cbd6f864b015f7571f73b59dfd`.\n\n## What Was Not Tested\n\nI did not perform a live Gemini CLI OAuth login against a real Google account. That would depend on external account state and local browser/device auth state. This proof exercises the deterministic resolver, forwarding, env clearing, queued/atomic auth-home file staging, default registration, SDK contract, metadata cleanup, docs-baseline, and upstream merge conflict boundaries in-process.\n\nI did not retest the full repository test suite. The focused suite covers the files and behavior changed in this PR, including the review finding repairs, the Plugin SDK API baseline check, and the latest upstream merge/queued-staging resolution.\n\n## Tests\n\nAI-assisted: yes.",
